Time Complexity:
O(m × n)

Space Complexity:
O(1)    // Ignoring the output list
         // O(m × n) if the output list is considered

Approach:
1. Initialize four boundaries: top, bottom, left, and right
2. Traverse from left to right along the top row and increment top
3. Traverse from top to bottom along the right column and decrement right
4. If rows remain, traverse from right to left along the bottom row and decrement bottom
5. If columns remain, traverse from bottom to top along the left column and increment left
6. Repeat the process while left ≤ right and top ≤ bottom
7. Store each visited element in the result list
8. Return the result list





class Solution {
    public List<Integer> spiralOrder(int[][] matrix) {
        ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();
        int top = 0;
        int bottom = matrix.length - 1;
        int left = 0;
        int right = matrix[0].length - 1;

        while (left <= right && top <= bottom) {
            //left--->right
            for (int i = left; i <= right; i++) {
                list.add(matrix[top][i]);
            }
            top++;

            //top--->bottom
            for (int i = top; i <= bottom; i++) {
                list.add(matrix[i][right]);
            }
            right--;

            //right--->left
            if (top <= bottom) {
                for (int i = right; i >= left; i--) {
                    list.add(matrix[bottom][i]);
                }
            }
            bottom--;

            //bottom--->top
            if (left <= right) {
                for (int i = bottom; i >= top; i--) {
                    list.add(matrix[i][left]);
                }
            }
            left++;
        }
        return list;
    }
}
